eval/run1/*.jsonl, eval/run2/*.jsonl (except eval/run2/clean_dev.jsonl)
  Original work written for this repository by Claude agents (not by native
  speakers), licensed with it (AGPL-3.0-or-later). No external text or dataset
  was copied. Rows are (input, refs, kind, class): kind is positive (must
  change), negative (must stay) or clean-style negatives; refs lists every
  output that counts as right. Operations: tidy, numbers, addresses and
  commands in en/fr/de/es, casing and emoji in en (run 1 only).
  run1 is the corpus the model arms were developed against, so it is not
  blind. run2 was written after every arm was frozen by an author that had
  not seen run1's failures: it is the blind corpus. Both share their authors'
  blind spots and the English rule-shaped references (commands, casing, emoji)
  were checked against the Rust rules they grade. Findings and caveats:
  server/.kb/text-processing-evaluation.md.

eval/run3/tidy_*.jsonl
  Original work written for this repository by a Claude agent (not by native
  speakers), licensed with it (AGPL-3.0-or-later), 48 items per language in
  en/fr/de/es: phrase restarts, repairs introduced by "actually" and its
  family (plutot, eigentlich, mejor dicho), mixed and multi-sentence
  disfluencies, and legitimate uses that must stay. Written with the
  multilingual tagger's training data fixed but its scores unseen, by an
  author that saw no training code; it grades breaks on run2's clean
  sentences.

eval/run2/clean_dev.jsonl
  Derived from Google FLEURS dev transcriptions (en_us, fr_fr, de_de, es_419;
  the raw cased, punctuated column), redistributed under the original licence.
  Source:  https://huggingface.co/datasets/google/fleurs
  Licence: CC-BY-4.0  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
  Inputs:  data/en_us/dev.tsv  sha256 9d57ee7e91e9d4c92edb39f6bbea668ef8dc2a3ff96eb510d5580b2ad05d17ec
           data/fr_fr/dev.tsv  sha256 3e0b792358c1cb4a426fe1c18fc1571d5406b390d738a2ed1bfd3c8b9d28de44
           data/de_de/dev.tsv  sha256 055b6ddecc9ad493d9ead86babe3ebe225148dd3c174fa6f95cb83a4f9586e18
           data/es_419/dev.tsv sha256 352b2a5f03f02fe752254fab737f76519963650f4630d2fb63957177aeec927f
  100 sentences per language of 5 to 35 words, in a seeded shuffle (seed
  20261125), after dropping any whose letters-only form occurs in any
  training or development text of any arm or in the clean_en and
  translate_en_<l> slices. The 400 rows are the clean sentences of run2:
  every operation is graded on a copy of its language's 100.
